\section{Appendix A: Full Sturm--Liouville Derivation}

In this appendix we present the complete derivation of the Sturm--Liouville (SL)
eigenvalue problem governing the Kaluza--Klein (KK) tower in the STME-RS-A
framework. The anharmonic bulk potential modifies the effective SL operator and
produces non-equidistant KK masses.

\subsection{Scalar Action and Equation of Motion}

The scalar action is
\begin{equation}
S_\Phi = \int d^4x \int_0^L dy \sqrt{-g}
\left[
-\frac{1}{2}g^{MN}\partial_M\Phi\partial_N\Phi
- V(\Phi)
\right],
\end{equation}
with metric
\begin{equation}
ds^2 = e^{-2k|y|}\eta_{\mu\nu}dx^\mu dx^\nu + dy^2.
\end{equation}

The equation of motion is
\begin{equation}
\frac{1}{\sqrt{-g}}\partial_M\left(\sqrt{-g}g^{MN}\partial_N\Phi\right)
= \frac{dV}{d\Phi}.
\end{equation}

\subsection{KK Decomposition}

We expand the scalar field as
\begin{equation}
\Phi(x,y) = \sum_{n=0}^{\infty} \phi_n(x) f_n(y),
\end{equation}
where $\phi_n(x)$ are four-dimensional fields and $f_n(y)$ are extra-dimensional
profiles.

The equation of motion becomes
\begin{equation}
e^{2ky}\partial_y\left(e^{-4ky}\partial_y f_n\right)
+ e^{-2ky} m_n^2 f_n
= \frac{d^2V}{d\Phi^2} f_n.
\end{equation}

\subsection{Sturm--Liouville Form}

We rewrite the equation in SL form:
\begin{equation}
-\frac{d}{dy}\left(p(y)\frac{df_n}{dy}\right)
+ q(y) f_n = m_n^2 w(y) f_n,
\end{equation}
with
\begin{align}
p(y) &= e^{-4ky}, \\
q(y) &= e^{-4ky} \frac{d^2V}{d\Phi^2}, \\
w(y) &= e^{-2ky}.
\end{align}

