\subsection{Boundary Conditions}

The boundary conditions follow from brane-localized potentials:
\begin{align}
\left.\partial_y f_n\right|_{y=0} &= \alpha_{\text{UV}} f_n(0), \\
\left.\partial_y f_n\right|_{y=L} &= -\alpha_{\text{IR}} f_n(L),
\end{align}
where $\alpha_{\text{UV}}$ and $\alpha_{\text{IR}}$ depend on brane potentials.

\subsection{Orthogonality}

The SL structure ensures orthogonality:
\begin{equation}
\int_0^L dy\, w(y) f_n(y) f_m(y) = \delta_{nm}.
\end{equation}

\subsection{Numerical Solution}

We discretize the SL equation using a second-order finite-difference scheme:
\begin{equation}
-\frac{p_{i+1/2}(f_{i+1}-f_i) - p_{i-1/2}(f_i - f_{i-1})}{\Delta y^2}
+ q_i f_i = m_n^2 w_i f_i.
\end{equation}

The resulting matrix eigenvalue problem yields numerical KK masses.

